{"availability":"available","full":"FatMii/nacos-web-config","name":"nacos-web-config","description":"Push whitelisted Nacos JSON configs to the browser over HTTP/SSE (Spring Boot starter + Browser SDK)","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-09T08:32:23Z","updated":"2026-10-08T06:37:00Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fatmii.github.io/nacos-web-config/","topics":["config","feature-flags","java","nacos","spring-boot","sse","typescript"],"demo":"https://fatmii.github.io/nacos-web-config/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:51.926Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:51.926Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:51.926Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:51.926Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Let the browser safely receive only the Nacos JSON configs you allow. Change a config, and the page updates.","0.1.0 is on Maven Central and npm. The quick start below installs from those registries.","Publish in Nacos — same-origin SSE pushes to the page (live recording)"],"features":["Do not put the password in the frontend. Anyone can see it in DevTools. A stolen Nacos account can change or delete configs, not only read them.","You cannot open just one config. Nacos authorizes by namespace. There is no switch for “the page may read only this one; leave the rest alone.”","Opening it to the public is risky. Anyone can hammer it. If it goes down, every backend that depends on it is affected."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FatMii/nacos-web-config/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2ec9045898f8da84cce279c651acb50842ccd1f860303815c82ef1588b6a34ec","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:52.024Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:52.024Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Let the browser safely receive only the Nacos JSON configs you allow. Change a config, and the page updates.","sourceUrl":"https://gith